under Apache License 2.0.
https://github.com/samuel-vitorino/sopro
https://huggingface.co/samuel-vitorino/sopro-v2-turbo
Source model revision: f747f9edfb7b0233a3b7105af3a75603a7213d26
LiteRT package revision: b1d2073b8111950ebf35614f4fd70b01ddaac3fb

This application ports host DSP, SentencePiece tokenization, sampling, packed
attention-cache management, acoustic integration and waveform reconstruction
to Kotlin. Conversion changes retain the model formulas while using static
shapes, explicit host inputs, digit-logit outputs and equivalent tensor layouts.

SentencePiece behavior is implemented against the Apache-2.0 reference library.
https://github.com/google/sentencepiece/tree/v0.2.2
The Python reference package is a development tool, not an Android dependency.

The default demo reference is voice-donations/0a67.wav from kyutai/tts-voices,
revision 323332d33f997de8394f24a193e1a76df720e01a, licensed CC0 1.0.
https://huggingface.co/kyutai/tts-voices/tree/323332d33f997de8394f24a193e1a76df720e01a/voice-donations
The sample fetches this asset separately; source staging does not include audio.

LiteRT 2.2.0, AndroidX, Compose Material 1 and Kotlin retain their respective
Apache-2.0 notices and licenses. Gradle wrapper files retain their original
license headers. Component license texts and source links are in licenses/.
